---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Write one setting of specforge.json, admitted by its declared type; never a secret

Usage: specforge settings set [OPTIONS] <EXTENSION> <NAME> [VALUE]...

Arguments:
  <EXTENSION>
          The extension, as `specforge settings` lists it

  <NAME>
          The setting's name, or a family's key (`models.planning`)

  [VALUE]...
          The value; a list takes every remaining word as an item

Options:
      --value-json <JSON>
          The value as one JSON document (a block, a list of blocks)

      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --dry-run
          Report what would be written; write nothing

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help
